<h2>1. Submagic — Best All-in-One for Captions and Clips</h2>
<p>Submagic does the two things a shorts workflow needs in one pass: word-level animated captions, and Magic Clips, which scans a long recording for highlights and cuts them into vertical clips you can publish to TikTok and Reels from the editor. Captions are supported in 123 languages, and exports run from 1080p30 on Starter to 4K60 on Business.</p>
<p>The plan structure is the thing to read carefully: Starter is $19/month ($12/month billed yearly) for 45 credits, which Submagic converts to about 15 captioned videos or 5 Magic Clips. Pro is $39/month ($23 yearly) for 120 credits (about 40 videos or 15 clips); Business is $69/month ($41 yearly) for 300 credits (about 100 videos or 37 clips). A Magic Clip costs more credits than a plain captioned video, and Starter caps each video at 2 minutes.</p>

