<h2>4. Descript — Best for Talking-Head Source Video</h2>
<p>Most shorts start life as a long, messy recording — a podcast, an interview, a screen-share tutorial. Descript cleans that source better than a clipper does: edit the transcript to cut the video, remove filler words automatically, and let Studio Sound fix room noise before a single clip is cut. Create Clips then handles the vertical conversion.</p>
<p>Free covers 60 media minutes a month at 720p; Hobbyist is $16/month billed annually ($24 monthly) for 600 minutes and 1080p; Creator is $24/month annual ($35 monthly) for 1,800 minutes and 4K. Media minutes are the budget unit, so a weekly hour-long podcast uses about half of Hobbyist's allowance on the source file alone.</p>

